3d-christmasstarbox is set up
Saved to environment
runs-on: windows
# One-time setup (e.g., install system tools, global CLIs).
initialize: |
  choco install openscad -y --no-progress
  choco install make -y --no-progress
knowledge:
  - name: render-stls
    contents: |
      make OPENSCAD="C:/Program Files/OpenSCAD/openscad.com"
      # Renders all 12 STLs (3 parts x 4 variants); `make <variant>` for one variant.
      # Use openscad.com (console wrapper), not openscad.exe, for single renders:
      # & "C:\Program Files\OpenSCAD\openscad.com" -o flat_front.stl -D 'part=\"front\"' star_box_flat.scad
 

Makefile added to PR #5 — make renders all 12 STLs (<variant>_<part>.stl), make <variant> one variant, OPENSCAD= to override the binary. All 12 regenerated and committed with the new naming (old front/back/base.stl removed): https://github.com/ranaur/3d-christmasstarbox/pull/5

Also sent a blueprint suggestion adding GNU make for future sessions.


